WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.777
Inference memory has at least two important components.

00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:11.672
Model weight memory is mostly determined by the number of parameters and the precision used to store them.

00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:16.632
That part is relatively fixed once the checkpoint and precision are chosen.

00:00:16.632 --> 00:00:19.492
K V cache memory behaves differently.

00:00:19.492 --> 00:00:26.772
It grows with sequence length, batch size, layer count, K V heads, head dimension, and precision.

00:00:26.772 --> 00:00:34.221
A model can fit its weights and still run out of memory when the context or concurrency grows.
